{"result":"{
  "id": "18827",
  "key": "SFCC-463",
  "summary": "Price Display Consistency — PWA Rendering Across All Surfaces",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper, \n**I want** to see prices displayed consistently in my local currency across every surface of the site, \n**so that** I always see the correct price regardless of where I am browsing.\n\nThe PWA must render the correct price consistently across: PLP, PDP, cart, wishlist, recommended product tiles, order history, recently viewed and checkout. The price source is either the SFCC pricebook for that storefront and currency, or — where no SFCC pricebook exists for the shopper's currency — the Global-e converted price derived from the base pricebook.\n\nThis is a PWA Kit frontend story. Currency display formatting rules (symbol, decimal places, separators) are configured in BM per [SFCC-46](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-46). \nCountry-to-currency mapping is configured per [SFCC-44](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-44). This story ensures the PWA applies those rules consistently across all surfaces.\n\n\n\nReference Image (Figma is leading)\n\n![\"image-20260901-052147.png\"](image-20260901-052147.png)\n\n![\"image-20260901-052244.png\"](image-20260901-052244.png)",
  "status": {
    "name": "Tech design",
    "category": "To Do",
    "color": "blue-gray"
  },
  "labels": [
    "Custom",
    "PRC-08",
    "PRC-33",
    "Squad-A"
  ],
  "customfield_10231": {
    "value": "# Given a Shopper's country is mapped to a specific currency, when they view a product tile on the PLP, then the price is displayed in the correct currency with the correct formatting.\n# Given a Shopper views a PDP, when the price renders, then the same price and formatting is shown as on the PLP product tile.\n# Given a Shopper views the cart, when line items and order summary render, then all prices are displayed in the correct currency with consistent formatting.\n# Given a Shopper views their wishlist, when product tile prices render, then the correct currency and formatting is applied.\n# Given a Shopper views recommended product tiles, when prices render, then the correct currency and formatting is applied.\n# Given a Shopper views their order history, when order amounts render, then prices are shown in the currency that was active at the time of order.\n# Given a Shopper proceeds to checkout, when prices render throughout the checkout flow, then the correct currency and formatting is applied consistently.\n# Given the formatting rules for a currency are updated in BM, when the storefront renders prices, then the updated formatting is reflected across all surfaces without a code deployment."
  }
}"}
